# Test_Movement

// Test conversations of the movement test scene. Characters: Elder, Messenger.
// Tags: "forced" starts when the player walks into a zone, "optional" needs the interact button.

[forced_intro | forced]
Messenger (happy): Wait! You walked into my zone, so this dialogue starts by itself.
Messenger (neutral): Forced dialogues are for story moments. Optional ones are for chatting with townsfolk.
Messenger (sad): That is all I had to say. Safe travels.

=========

[optional_chat | optional]
// Story flags demo: "elder_trust" is set by the choice at the end of this conversation and read here on the next visit.
@if elder_trust >= 1
Elder (happy): Good to see you again, friend!
@end
Elder (neutral): Hello, traveler. This is the optional dialogue: you pressed the interact button to talk to me.
Elder (happy): The text appears letter by letter, with longer pauses after commas, and even longer after full stops.
Messenger (angry): Press <color=#ffd060>Space</color> while I am talking and the whole line shows at once!
Elder (sad): Press it again to continue... and once more to close this box.
> A line without a name is narration: no name plate, portrait or voice.
Elder (neutral): One last thing, traveler. Will you help me find my lost bell?
@choice
- Of course, I will. => @set helped_elder @add elder_trust 1 @quest start find_bell
- Maybe later. => @set refused_elder
- Tell me more first. => @goto elder_bell_story

@if helped_elder
Elder (happy): Wonderful! You have my thanks.
@else
Elder (sad): I understand. Talk to me again if you change your mind.
@end

=========

[elder_bell_story | optional]
// Reached with "@goto" from the choice above.
Elder (sad): The bell rang from the old tower every morning, until the day the roof fell.
Elder (neutral): Now you know. Talk to me again if you want to help.

=========

[sign_welcome | optional]
// No speaker name: signs use narration lines, so the box is centered with no portrait.
> Welcome to the test area. Walk into the forced zone to the south-west, or talk to the block to the east.
> Press Space to close this sign.

=========

[cutscene_demo | forced]
// Cutscene demo: @commands run in order, the dialogue box hides while they run.
@quest start deliver_message
@fade out 0.6
@wait 0.3
@face Messenger north
@fade in 0.6
Messenger (happy): Hold on, traveler! This is a cutscene: the screen faded out and back in by itself.
@camera focus Elder 1.2
@wait 0.6
Messenger (neutral): The camera just moved to the Elder. Commands go inside the same .dialogue file.
@camera follow Player 0.8
@move Messenger -3.5 -6
@face Messenger west
Messenger (sad): I walked here on my own. Safe travels.
@quest complete deliver_message
// Scene change: loads Test_House, puts the player on its "door" spawn point and continues with "house_intro".
// Delete this line to end the demo here instead.
@scene Test_House door house_intro

=========

[violet_chat | optional]
// Portrait test: every expression of Violet and of the Protagonist appears at least once.
Violet (neutral): ...Oh. It's you.
Protagonist (neutral): Hey, Violet. Do you have a minute?
Violet (happy): Always. You're the only one who asks.
Protagonist (happy): That's not true. Everybody likes you.
Violet (sad): Do they? Sometimes it feels like they only look at me when something goes wrong.
Protagonist (angry): Then they are not paying attention!
Violet (angry): Don't shout. I'm not made of glass.
Protagonist (scared): Sorry! I did not mean to... I just...
Violet (scared): Wait. Did you hear that?
Protagonist (shocked): Hear what? I did not hear anything.
Violet (neutral): Good. Forget it. It was nothing.
> End of the portrait test.

=========

[kate_chat | optional]
// Portrait test: every expression of Kate and of the Protagonist appears at least once.
Kate (neutral): Oh, hi. I was just looking at the ground. There are some really interesting rocks here.
Protagonist (neutral): Rocks. Right. You said that yesterday too.
Kate (happy): And they were still interesting! Do you want to see this one?
Protagonist (happy): Okay, okay. Show me.
Kate (sad): ...It was a better rock before I picked it up. It looked different on the ground.
Protagonist (scared): Kate, why is it glowing?
Kate (scared): I do not know! I did not do anything, I swear!
Protagonist (angry): Put it down. Now.
Kate (angry): Do not tell me what to do! It is my rock!
Protagonist (shocked): Fine, fine. Just do not drop it on my foot.
Kate (neutral): ...Okay. I put it back. Happy now?
> End of the portrait test.

=========

[alice_chat | optional]
// Portrait test: every expression of Alice and of the Protagonist appears at least once.
Alice (neutral): You are late. Again.
Protagonist (neutral): I am not late. You are just always early.
Alice (happy): That is the same thing, only more flattering to me.
Protagonist (happy): Fine. You win. What are you doing out here?
Alice (sad): Running. It is the only thing that makes the world feel slow enough.
Protagonist (scared): Alice, you were standing next to me a second ago. Where did you go?
Alice (scared): I do not know. I only blinked and the road was behind me.
Protagonist (shocked): That is not normal, even for you.
Alice (angry): Do not say that like I am a freak!
Protagonist (angry): I did not mean it like that, and you know it.
Alice (neutral): ...Yeah. I know. Sorry.
> End of the portrait test.

=========

[gabe_chat | optional]
// Portrait test: every expression of Gabe and of the Protagonist appears at least once.
Gabe (neutral): Hey. Everyone else is busy, so I figured I would check on you.
Protagonist (neutral): I am fine. You do not have to do that.
Gabe (happy): I know. That is why it counts.
Protagonist (happy): You are impossible, you know that?
Gabe (sad): Sometimes I think I am the only one who is not scared of what is coming.
Protagonist (scared): Gabe, behind you!
Gabe (scared): What? Where?! ...Oh. It is just a branch.
Protagonist (shocked): You almost gave me a heart attack.
Gabe (angry): I almost gave myself one! Do not do that to me!
Protagonist (angry): Then stop making me worry about you.
Gabe (neutral): ...Deal. Come on, let us go back.
> End of the portrait test.
